 #edb/ref 1031 "Completing the Square With Leading Coefficients" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051078 #edb/ref 1033 3824 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186051078 #edb/ref 1034 1.20001426448432 #edb/ref 17592186045436] [17592186051078 #edb/ref 1035 #uuid "7f1179a4-dcfa-50b2-b12b-655dfefa3ff3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082517 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186082518 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082517 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186082519 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082517 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186506018 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082517 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186506038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082517 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186506353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082517 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082517 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082517 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186506038 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082517 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "a853deee-5932-5d06-a167-17ff4c201b5f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082518 #edb/ref 1080 "(-1,-3)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082518 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082518 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "9fa64c84-d1cf-51ed-ab94-685452dba6d3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082519 #edb/ref 1080 "(3,-1)" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082519 #edb/ref 1082 #edb/ref 17592186045498 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186082519 #edb/ref 1083 #uuid "ae2c79a9-150f-5318-8256-6ef4a7ab390b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083007 #edb/ref 1069 "e-5354" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083007 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the center of the hyperbola \n$4 y^2  - 10 x^2 - 8 y  - 40 x  = 76?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083007 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e930a29a-6adf-5aaa-9b44-86dd8d570ae7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083007 #edb/ref 1074 "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}-10{x}^{2}-8y-40x & =76 \\\\ 4{y}^{2}-8y-10{x}^{2}-40x & =76 \\\\ 4[{y}^{2}-2y]-10[{x}^{2}+4x] & =76 \\\\ 4[(y-1)^{2}-1]-10[(x+2)^{2}-4] & =76 \\\\ 4(y-1)^{2}-4-10(x+2)^{2}+40 & =76 \\\\ 4(y-1)^{2}-10(x+2)^{2} & =76-40+4 \\\\ 4(y-1)^{2}-10(x+2)^{2} & =40 \\\\ \\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{10}-\\frac{(x+2)^{2}}{4} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the center is $(-2,1)$." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083078 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6775" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083078 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{9} - \\dfrac{(y-2)^2}{4} = 1 ?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083078 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0caa1041-a564-5428-9838-20cea32fdf17" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083078 #edb/ref 1074 "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h = 1$ and $k = 2.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(1,2).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083079 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6776" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083079 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the center of the hyperbola $\\dfrac{(y+3)^2}{16} - \\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{9} = 1 ?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083079 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8e31f5b5-ff87-5c45-b143-66dfdcb4ab8c" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083079 #edb/ref 1074 "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-k)^2}{a^2} - \\dfrac{(x-h)^2}{b^2}=1.\n$$\n\nNote that the given equation can be rewritten as follows:\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{(y-(-3))^2}{16} - \\dfrac{(x-1)^2}{9}=1\n$$\n\nIn this case, we have $h = 1$ and $k=-3.$\n\nTherefore, the center of the hyperbola is $(1,-3).$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083080 #edb/ref 1069 "e-6777" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186083080 #edb/ref 1071 "What is the center of the hyperbola \n![](images/e1/